<%# locals: (text:) %>
<%# A few words that say something about a bank transaction needs a second look, such as "Doesn't add up", "Deleted in Splitwise" or "Removed by TD Canada Trust": a `badge-warning`, whose words carry the meaning and never the colour. A bank's name can be long, so on a narrow row it wraps inside its pill (`h-auto`) rather than widening the row and crushing the date and the amount; a short one stays on one line. %>
<span class="badge badge-warning badge-sm h-auto max-w-full py-0.5 text-start"><%= text %></span>
